# Amendment 1.0.1: F10/F11 prerequisite review budgets

This amendment permits two narrowly bounded legacy prerequisite adoptions to be reviewed above the usual 400 handwritten production lines. F10 receives a 420-production/900-authored cap; F11 receives a 460-production/900-authored cap. These are source review budgets. They establish no resource capacity, application support, native correspondence, execution result or feature acceptance.

The amendment is prepared against main `f774944bf8da6eb03881ee4c37046e879c222fff` and changes `SYSON-RUST-COMPLETION/1.0.0` to `SYSON-RUST-COMPLETION/1.0.1`. It takes effect only after independent review, explicit adoption and coordinator refresh of the contract hash lock. Freeze the exact proposed source composition before any F10/F11 execution. A drafted amendment, its hashes and previous test transcripts do not satisfy that prerequisite.

## Exact source bounds

| Legacy prerequisite | Donor | Observed production | Observed Rust tests | Observed Rust authored total | Review cap |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| F10, #25, `syson-ast-values` | `48ee69e41c4f29346f1d95075278d84aefc48057` | 409 | 372 | 781 | 420 production / 900 authored |
| F11, #40, `syson-ast-adapter` | `ca1c4b3ab364db7dc9da835c66cba72912c3417f` | 447 | 358 | 805 | 460 production / 900 authored |

Observed authored totals above are the donor Rust implementation plus Rust tests. Review of the exact adoption must also account for any additional authored implementation and tests. The caps apply only to these donor-derived prerequisite adoptions; they do not raise any current unit's general budget. Any additional code or changed dependency input requires review in the exact composition, even when the count remains below the cap. Exceeding a cap requires another reviewed disposition or named split before execution. Cosmetic compression and removal of tests or behavior cannot satisfy a cap.

