F11's 173 generated keyword lines in `reserved.rs` remain separately reviewed generated source, excluded from handwritten implementation and authored-code budgets under the existing policy. Review their source derivation and exact bytes; classifying them as generated does not establish lexical completeness or native parity.

## Provenance and rationale

F10's retained `porting/follow-ons/F10/source-contract.json` at its donor is Git blob `0d6d3c668787efed8188eab9b778abb549d65556`, SHA-256 `ed46c9000e71d2e4319954736db12d9c39e9f9a8ade80151edb2f54eff77192d`. Its crate notice is blob `7aa43f1dd2abaee3b126c51ae4c0798194ad4d29`, SHA-256 `5f2e54789e7420959f5f3b2ef37054aff4a7d04aef72e75dbb7b694cd9607011`. These preserve the embedded Langium primitive-conversion, candidate Syside naming and SysON literal-spelling provenance, with their existing correspondence and license qualifications.

F11's retained `porting/follow-ons/F11/source-manifest.json` at its donor is Git blob `f3ab5321eb70151c48c7cc54d453e9a22a209ae1`, SHA-256 `e0dbf8f1ad21c6bc734f2abe7834aaef998b68e0d098fc9e2d0ec49571892dab`. Its crate notice is blob `fe82e42921cdb18cb4921e19b512dc9aadcafbd1`, SHA-256 `1313dad4470bea7182a034a027e7ad1efb0f09c914c82a2f8057cd505d61f106`. These bind the retained Syside candidate `1326f234cae23b0e4777d5a48a069b17e9e332f1` and finite source-shaped construction obligations. Preserve all original notices and source qualifications; hashes prove the selected bytes, not native behavior.

The source review found cohesive alternatives: F10 could separate name sanitation from primitive dispatch; F11 could separate finite scanning/parsing from AST emission. This amendment instead retains the existing APIs and implementation boundaries for the two finite prerequisites. The excess is nine production lines for F10 and 47 for F11, while both retain complete test suites within 900 authored lines. Review the conversion/error/span rules and finite construction/default/reference behavior together, without introducing another interface solely to meet the default line budget. This rationale grants no exception to another unit or future behavior family.

## Compatibility and unchanged acceptance obligations

No API, behavior, source obligation, dependency, ownership, case assignment, performance policy or hold changes. Preserve all 16 original F10 tests and all 13 original F11 tests, plus every required downstream case and historical failed attempt. Earlier source-derived or local evidence retains its original scope and candidate; this amendment does not promote any record or make a native source claim. The 778 current review units and 55 historical implementation/evidence records remain unchanged, and no IDs are added.

The real finite-import consuming path remains F08 #23 -> F10 #25 -> F11 #40 -> F13 #50 with F04 #47 -> F14 #52, followed by the declared F33/#63/I01/RR02/RR05 callers. F14 must use the actual adapter, primitive converter, reflection metadata, AST kernel, linker, explicit registry and selected-model transaction. Its graph-free implementation does not remove prerequisite admission, actual caller, identity, atomicity, cancellation, failure, commit/cancel/undo, save/reopen, native comparison or applicable UI/lifecycle/resource gates.

F01 #48 and F05 #54 retain their held initializer-graph authority gates. F33 #55 retains the mandatory `actual_f05_external_view_projection_roundtrips_all_resources` case and its F05 dependency. No mock replacement, test omission or inference that a hold ended is permitted. Native/artifact closure, durable lifecycle, full feature acceptance and production deployment remain separate requirements.

